 The first read of a record or of a category listing goes to the backend. Later reads of the same thing are answered
 from memory for `ttl` seconds and cost no query. Records handed out are copies.
 
+A change made with `update` is seen by the very next read: `update` drops the cached record and the cached listing
+of every category the product was in or is in now, so `get`, `get_many` and `list_category` never return the value
+from before the update. Everything else stays cached.
+
